{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPZVrqpdRRrsTq83SKEk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016P5dY32eqBJGAbyxV635Tb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-976\\docs\\reviews\\wi-976\\016-ADJUDICATE-9d6ad4c.md","content":"# WI-976 checkpoint sitting at 9d6ad4c\n\n## amendment\n\nThis re-sits the whole set after sitting 015 (`015-ADJUDICATE-91ed238.md`), which blessed every MEANING row on its released rung except LLR-273. Since 015's commit (ff639cbe5), two registry changes have landed:\n- LLR-273's Detail drops the module qualifier and keeps the approved symbol, as 015 worded the return;\n- TC-211's Inputs now name this sitting's brief and verdict.\n\nThis sitting's brief, `016-ADJUDICATE-9d6ad4c.brief.md`, is committed, and it still shows LLR-297 and TC-312 as removals. `trace.py --strict` exits 0. No other row text has moved since 015, so its rulings stand on the same reasons.\n\nTen rows changed MEANING and one only CLARITY. I would bless all nine MEANING rows on their released rungs. SN-036 is held and goes to the owner, and no CLARITY row shares its registry. Nothing on a released rung is left drifted and unblessed, so the act turn can take every registry this sitting rules except the stakeholder table, which is the owner's.\n\n- [MEANING] SN-036 Acceptance -> before: a machine-readable per-decomposition record and a check reporting a missing perspective -> after: each round reviewed against every applicable declared perspective, the review record naming each outcome, adequacy left to independent review -> not the same: a record and a check become a reviewed round. The rung is held. As at sittings 011, 012 and 015, I recommend it to the owner: it is the owner's 2026-09-06 ruling verbatim, an observable condition that names no instrument.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-297 (removed) -> before: the per-decomposition perspective record, with its derived applicabi